# Web vs mobile scope

This repo is a monorepo. A request to ship a feature in a **web** app is **not**
a request to implement it in the mobile apps.

## Default

When asked to add, ship, or change a feature in:

- `apps/web` (diner web)
- `apps/dashboard` (partner/admin web)

Do **not** also implement it in:

- `apps/mobile` (diner Expo)
- `apps/merchant-mobile` (partner Expo)

Do not copy screens, components, navigation, copy, or UX from web into the
mobile apps. Mobile has a separate UI system; porting web UI produces poor
mobile UX.

## Exceptions

Touch a mobile app only when the user **explicitly** names it (`apps/mobile`,
`apps/merchant-mobile`, diner app, merchant app, Expo, or "mobile").

API (`apps/api`) and shared packages may still change if the web feature needs
them. That is not permission to add mobile client UI.

## Examples

- "Ship this on the website" / "add this to the web app" → `apps/web` only
- "Add this in Partner Hub / dashboard" → `apps/dashboard` only
- "Also add it to the diner app" → then `apps/mobile` is in scope
